cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  manuscript it implements.
title: >-
  bircpg: reference implementation of bio-inspired resource-constrained
  potential games for adaptive coordination in autonomous multi-agent systems
abstract: >-
  Implements and verifies the formal model, equilibrium analysis and
  prospective evaluation protocol of the manuscript "Bio-Inspired
  Resource-Constrained Potential Games for Adaptive Coordination in
  Autonomous Multi-Agent Systems". The Level I layer is exact: the
  potential identity, the approximate-equilibrium certificate and the
  stationary law are checked in rational arithmetic, and the constructed
  two-agent example of Section 6 is reproduced exactly. No experiment
  reported in the manuscript has been executed, and the package makes no
  empirical performance claim.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "REPLACE BEFORE DEPOSITION: public repository URL"
keywords:
  - potential games
  - computational game theory
  - autonomous agents
  - resource-constrained coordination
  - bounded rationality
  - stigmergy
  - Nash equilibrium
  - bio-inspired control
